# prefixsid-malformed-receive -- RFC 8669 Section 6 and RFC 9252 Section 7, a received Prefix-SID
# judged by the family of the routes it is attached to, from a peer's socket to another peer's.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC8669-6-1 negative -- on IPv4 labeled unicast a Prefix-SID holding a Label-Index TLV of length 6, and an empty Prefix-SID, are discarded: the route is relayed without attribute 40.
# RFC requirement: RFC8669-4.1-2 negative -- on IPv4 labeled unicast a Prefix-SID holding no Label-Index TLV (only an Originator SRGB TLV) is invalid and discarded: the route is relayed without attribute 40.
# RFC requirement: RFC8669-3.1-2 positive -- on IPv4 VPN a Label-Index TLV of length 6 is ignored: attribute 40 is relayed octet-equal.
# RFC requirement: RFC8669-3-1 positive -- on IPv4 VPN a Label-Index TLV with non-zero Reserved and Flags is relayed octet-equal, not cleared.
# RFC requirement: RFC9252-3.4-1 negative -- on IPv4 VPN a re-announcement whose SRv6 L3 Service TLV overruns attribute 40 is treat-as-withdraw: the relay sends a withdrawal of the route it relayed before.
#
# RFC 8669 Section 6: "a malformed BGP Prefix-SID attribute is one that cannot be parsed due to
# not meeting the minimum attribute length requirement, containing a TLV length that doesn't
# conform to the length constraints for the TLV, or containing a TLV length that would extend
# beyond the end of the attribute", judged for a Prefix-SID "attached to an IPv4/ IPv6 Labeled
# Unicast prefix"; off labeled unicast the Label-Index and SRGB TLVs are unrecognized (Section
# 3.1: "It MUST be ignored when received for other BGP AFI/SAFI combinations."). RFC 9252
# Section 7: "The treat-as-withdraw action [RFC7606] MUST be performed when at least one
# malformed SRv6 Service TLV is present in the BGP Prefix-SID attribute." The judge is
# attribute.ClassifyPrefixSID, called from the RFC 7606 walk (validatePrefixSIDForRoutes in
# internal/component/bgp/message/rfc7606.go); the egress clear is clearTransmittedLabelIndex.
#
# EIGHT UPDATES from AS 65001, each one route; every route carries ORIGIN IGP, AS_PATH [65001] and
# MP_REACH_NLRI (labeled unicast: label 1000, next hop 1.1.1.1; VPN: label 2000, RD 65001:1, next
# hop 0:0:1.1.1.1), then attribute 40:
#   (a)  10.0.1.0/24 labeled unicast, Label-Index TLV of length 6        -> relayed without 40
#   (b1) 10.0.2.0/24 VPN, a valid SRv6 L3 Service TLV                    -> relayed as received
#   (b2) 10.0.2.0/24 VPN again, the L3 Service TLV length 39 over 34     -> relayed withdrawal
#   (c)  10.0.3.0/24 VPN, Label-Index of length 6 then a valid L3 TLV    -> relayed as received
#   (d)  10.0.4.0/24 labeled unicast, an Originator SRGB TLV only        -> relayed without 40
#   (e1) 10.0.5.0/24 labeled unicast, attribute 40 of length 0           -> relayed without 40
#   (e2) 10.0.6.0/24 VPN, attribute 40 of length 0                       -> relayed without 40
#   (f)  10.0.7.0/24 VPN, Label-Index of length 7, Reserved AA, Flags BBCC -> relayed as received
# "Relayed without 40" is ze's RFC 7606 attribute discard: attribute 40 leaves as an ATTR_TOMBSTONE
# (type 252, draft-mangin-idr-attr-tombstone-00) naming code 40 and the reason. (a) and (d) are
# stamped in place, the value zeroed past code and reason: reason 2 (invalid length) for (a),
# reason 3 (malformed value) for (d). An empty attribute has no room for the marker, so for (e1)
# and (e2) attribute 40 is removed and a 2-octet tombstone, 28 02, is appended.
# Each expectation is the UPDATE that left, compared octet for octet: a family-blind judge fails
# (c) and (f), a judge that never reads TLV lengths fails (a), (d) and (e), and an overrun read as
# attribute-discard leaves (b) installed, so no withdrawal arrives.
#
# WHY rs-client, accept-srv6-prefix-sid AND propagate-srv6-prefix-sid: as in
# prefixsid-duplicate-tlv-relay.ci, so the relayed frames differ from the received ones in
# attribute 40 alone.

stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=2
option=timeout:value=20s
option=bind:value=0.0.0.0
option=conn_map:value=remote-ip
option=await_eor:value=true

action=send:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0043020000002C4001010040020602010000FDE9800E1000010404010101010030003E810A0001C02809010006000000000000
action=send:conn=1:seq=2:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF006F02000000584001010040020602010000FDE9800E200001800C0000000000000000010101010070007D010000FDE9000000010A0002C028250500220001001E0020010DB800010000000000000000000000001300010006201010000000
action=send:conn=1:seq=3:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF006F02000000584001010040020602010000FDE9800E200001800C0000000000000000010101010070007D010000FDE9000000010A0002C028250500270001001E0020010DB800010000000000000000000000001300010006201010000000
